menu "Station: receiver supervisor"

    config STATION_TASK_STACK
        int "Supervisor task stack (bytes)"
        range 4096 16384
        default 8192
        help
            Internal RAM (the task writes settings). Detection, the profile
            apply and the command layer's session executor run on it.
            PROVISIONAL, to be confirmed on hardware from the task's stack
            high-water mark.

    config STATION_FLASH_RESTART_ALLOWANCE_S
        int "Receiver write, restart and reacquisition allowance for an update (s)"
        range 30 900
        default 180
        help
            Added to the transfer time at the loader baud (package size,
            10 bits per byte, plus 10 %) to estimate a receiver update's
            downtime for the confirmation dialog. Information only: it never
            gates an update. Refine from measured runs.

    config STATION_LIVE_VIEW_MIN
        int "Live view: window length (minutes)"
        range 1 60
        default 10
        help
            How long the live view stays open after the user opens it; the
            user can extend it. While it is open the receiver's
            satellite-in-view output is on (never saved), so it is kept
            short and closes by itself.

    config STATION_LIVE_VIEW_MAX_MIN
        int "Live view: longest window, extensions included (minutes)"
        range 10 240
        default 60

    config STATION_LIVE_VIEW_IDLE_S
        int "Live view: close when no admin client asked for it this long (s)"
        range 30 900
        default 120
        help
            The web API reports every live-view request; a window nobody
            looks at closes after this long and the receiver output it
            turned on is turned off again.

    config STATION_LIVE_VIEW_SKY_PERIOD_S
        int "Live view: satellite-in-view output period (s)"
        range 1 60
        default 5
        help
            Period of the receiver's satellite-in-view sentences while the
            live view is open (azimuth and elevation for the sky plot). A
            modest period keeps the extra load on the receiver link small
            next to the RTCM stream. PROVISIONAL, to be confirmed on
            hardware.

endmenu
